nd of material if you are  that could be a red flag to bookers so  thirdly  the material they're looking for is that  personal material  is that unique material i can tell you  from interviewing  so many bookers and late night bookers  specifically  is that they are looking for you  the comedian they're looking to learn  from you as a booker  especially late night they're looking  for a set  that they could write a sitcom about so  when you're doing a tight five-minute  set you want to pitch to bookers  you want to make sure you're doing a set  where it's personal it's unique to you  and you should be doing this anyway  writing material that's unique to you i  always put my comedy  through the filter of could someone else  say this  joke and it be just as funny if that's  the case  then i get rid of it i i kill the joke  it's not worth it  write in that personal material because  that's how you're going to find your  voice faster as well  a great quick way to find your voice is  to do personal material  do material that's unique to you your  own unique experiences your own unique  points of view your own unique opinions  all of those will help you to find your  voice  and find the bookers that want a book  comedian  oh that was a good tip if you found that  tip helpful go ahead and hit that  subscribe button  so more comments can find these tips now  the bonus tip here  as we're landing the plane and running  running low on time here  the bonus tip on how to actually contact  bookers  this is so simple  and overlooked in comedy and i can tell  you i've booked several shows and i've  interviewed a bunch of bookers  be professional when you contact a  booker  don't say yo hey here's uh  a link let me get some stage time be  professional  hey so and so i've heard great things  about your club i've heard great things  about your show  i'm comedian blank i have this  experience  i would love the opportunity to perform  on your show  at a date you see me a good fit for  b